WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.032
Raj: The guard clause rejects missing tenant values. An empty path component now fails closed.

2
00:00:07.032 --> 00:00:15.048
Lukas: That protects inputs, not every filesystem race. Use constrained directory handles for deletion too.

3
00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:22.585
Anika: I'll narrow the identity to tenant storage. Shared artifact directories won't grant deletion rights.

4
00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:29.809
Priya: Just to confirm, links are rejected, right? We're not silently following external targets.

5
00:00:29.809 --> 00:00:37.681
Hannah: Yes, and replacement races need explicit tests. A static path check isn't enough.

6
00:00:37.681 --> 00:00:44.521
Raj: I'm on it with the handle-based implementation. Maybe we'll need a platform-specific helper.

7
00:00:44.521 --> 00:00:52.225
Lukas: Review that helper before production use. Unsupported platforms must refuse deletion rather than fallback.

8
00:00:52.225 --> 00:01:00.410
Priya: Okay, make that an explicit action item. Hannah owns verification, Raj owns the implementation.

9
00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:08.714
Hannah: I'll preserve the evidence alongside test results. Reviewers can trace each protection to failure.

10
00:01:08.714 --> 00:01:16.250
Anika: Good, cleanup permissions stay suspended for now. Code approval alone won't unlock production access.

